Vendoring: a copy of the upstream modeling source at the pinned commit, with
three safety changes and nothing else:
  1. modeling_wavjepa.py passed config.extractor_config['conv_layers_spec'] to
     eval(). It now goes through parse_conv_layers_spec, which accepts only
     integer tuples and lists combined with "+" and "*", and refuses anything
     else.
  2. audio_extractor.py called eval() on strings it had just formatted, in a
     __repr__-style description. The products are now computed directly.
  3. types.py, which shadows the standard library module of that name, is
     renamed wavjepa_types.py, and its two importers are updated.
The model is loaded with trust_remote_code=False, local_files_only=True and
HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1. The entity's runtime path loads the student (context) encoder
only; the teacher and predictor are loaded only by the offline bake-off's
mismatch mode.

